# SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
# Qwen3.8-Flash-Next, the GPU driving no display.
# 131k at q8_0/q8_0, every expert in RAM, ubatch 512: 7 386 MiB of buffers, 9.3 tok/s short (9.85
# with -t 7), 8.3 at 31k, prompts at ~36 tok/s. The sparse-attention indexer takes ~13 B x CTX x UB of VRAM,
# which is what bounds the window: 262k needs q4_0/q4_0 and UB 256 (CTX=262144 KV_K=q4_0 KV_V=q4_0
# UB=256, 7.56 GB, same tg, prompts at ~29). See docs/qwen38-flash.md.
# The budget is by the rules in docs/agent.md#context-budget, not measured in a session. BUDGET is
# Bonsai's, not Qwen3.6's: at ~10 tok/s 8k of thinking is already ~14 minutes.
: "${MODEL:=qwen38-flash}"
: "${CTX:=131072}"
: "${CPU_MOE:=48}"
: "${UB:=512}"
: "${BUDGET:=8192}"
: "${MAX_TOKENS:=32000}"
: "${RESERVE_TOKENS:=32000}"
: "${KEEP_RECENT_TOKENS:=24000}"
# Its CUDA pool does not grow with depth (VRAM flat over a 110k fill, docs/qwen38-flash.md), so the
# fill's own peak is the attempt's: the 300 MiB margin for growth is not needed (T-075).
: "${BENCH_VRAM_MARGIN_MB:=150}"
